<p>North Korea said it carried out weapons tests on Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday, including ballistic missiles, as state media laid out a week of military trials and confirmed launches previously detected by South Korea&#x27;s military. The reported systems included a surface-to-surface tactical ballistic missile identified as the Hwasongpho-11 Ka, and North Korean media said some tests used missiles fitted with cluster-bomb warheads as Pyongyang pushed to expand its nuclear-capable forces. State media also said the tests involved an electromagnetic weapon system and a carbon-fibre bomb, widening the range of technologies North Korea says it is developing. The activity adds to regional security concerns because it comes on top of an already brisk launch pace this year: Le Monde reported that the latest trials brought the number of known ballistic missile tests by Pyongyang in 2026 to five.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Vc8BgHlEIaR7t5aN3uoC9KJCZHAs1P4JLQHmf6O26U1-jGgtFe51sn1hxp8-YYcdUZs1HasoMyzRojEPK1pDDkiRuUv45bMpfroJPJKLGx8ORMyWY3DIHqhltKUGN69d7is6LWmDX6u5l_tWi9VKHSIIdreD4opY3mcEmjndvszm-cieIOXKZz0BVV16dCGYc4G4T9jfEiLv5IH1-wVGIDtWk1Ft5Gq4aQaPz3jzLTkAH2b3C2jTJHrbBw' alt='A TV screen shows a file image of North Korea&#x27;s missile launch during a news program at Seoul Railway Station in Seoul, South Korea, Wednesday, April 8, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>North Korean state media: KCNA cast the week&#x27;s activity as part of a push to expand nuclear-capable forces, portraying the launches as weapons-development work rather than isolated shows of force. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/09/g-s1-116848/north-korea-says-its-latest-weapons-tests-included-missiles-with-cluster-bomb-warheads'>NPR</a>)</li><li>South Korean military: Seoul said the missiles came from North Korea&#x27;s eastern coastal area and described the event as a second round of launches in two days. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/north-korea-says-latest-tests-used-cluster-bomb-warhead-missiles-11331433#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: Le Monde emphasized the cumulative effect of the latest launches, saying they added to North Korea&#x27;s already active ballistic-missile testing pace in 2026. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/09/north-korea-tested-missiles-on-monday-tuesday-and-wednesday-state-media-confirms_6752249_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/09/north-korea-tested-missiles-on-monday-tuesday-and-wednesday-state-media-confirms_6752249_4.html'>North Korea tested missiles on Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday, state media confirms</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/09/g-s1-116848/north-korea-says-its-latest-weapons-tests-included-missiles-with-cluster-bomb-warheads'>North Korea says its latest weapons tests included missiles with cluster-bomb warheads</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/north-korea-says-latest-tests-used-cluster-bomb-warhead-missiles-11331433#publisher=newsstand'>North Korea Says Latest Tests Used Cluster-Bomb Warhead Missiles</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3349440/tests-electromagnetic-weapon-and-carbon-fibre-bomb-state-media'>North Korea tests electromagnetic weapon and carbon fibre bomb: state media</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20260409000351315'>The Korean Central News Agency reports that North Korea has tested various military technologies throughout the week, including a surface-to-surface missile tactical ballistic missile identified as Hwasongpho-11 Ka.</a> - yna.co.kr</li></ul>